From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Sun, 16 Aug 2026 09:20:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] hwcomposer: always pass the buffer to set_client_target

The slot cache added in "implement the usage of slot-based buffer cache"
passes a null target once a buffer has been seen before, leaving the slot
index as the only way for the composer to know which buffer is meant. That
relies on the composer keeping its own slot-indexed cache of buffers it has
already been handed.

Older HWC2 implementations do not, and the null is dereferenced instead. On
a Halium 9 device (Adreno, Android 9 vendor blobs) surface-manager dies on
the second frame:

  #0  hwc2_compat_display_set_client_target (libhwc2_compat_layer.so)
  #1  HWC2Window::present(HWComposerNativeWindowBuffer*) (libhwcomposer.so)
  #2  HWComposerNativeWindow::queueBuffer(BaseNativeWindowBuffer*, int)
  ...
  #10 eglSwapBuffers
  #12 QRhi::endFrame
      QSGRenderThread

which reads as a Qt or libhybris fault and is neither - the first frame is
fine, because the buffer is not in the cache yet and a real pointer is
passed. Only from the second frame on, when the cache hits, does the null
reach the composer.

Keep the slot bookkeeping, since the slot number is still what the composer
uses to identify the buffer, but always hand over the buffer as well.
Supplying a buffer for an already-cached slot is valid for every HWC2
implementation - the cache is an optimisation to avoid re-importing a
buffer, not a requirement to omit it - so this stays correct on newer
composers while working on older ones.

Upstream-Status: Pending [written against 41e7bda, intended for
mer-hybris/qt5-qpa-hwcomposer-plugin]
---
 hwcomposer_backend_v20.cpp | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

--- a/hwcomposer_backend_v20.cpp
+++ b/hwcomposer_backend_v20.cpp
@@ -207,7 +207,6 @@
     // Check if the current buffer is cached in any slots
     for (size_t i = 0; i < m_slotCache.size(); i++) {
         if (m_slotCache[i] == buffer) {
-            target = nullptr;
             slot = i;
             break;
         }
